# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-dram-case-display.rules (pkgs/dram-case-display, docs/case-display.md)
# The Antec Flux Pro's temperature panel, USB 2022:0522 (either hardware revision). Its usbfs
# node goes to the group dram-case-panel, which dram-case-display.service's dynamic user joins
# (others keep the default read-only access). TAG+="systemd" and SYSTEMD_ALIAS make a stable
# device unit, dev-dram_case_display.device, that the service BindsTo; SYSTEMD_WANTS starts the
# service when the panel appears. After 50-udev-default.rules (its MODE), before 99-systemd.rules.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="2022", ATTR{idProduct}=="0522", \
  GROUP="dram-case-panel", MODE="0664", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_ALIAS}="/dev/dram_case_display", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="dram-case-display.service"
